                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Overall in support here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "docs/mctp/Makefile",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "meson?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "docs/mctp/Makefile",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "No, I don't intend to convert this to meson. The `Makefile` does two things\n\n1. Download the TLA+ toolbox, which contains the model-checker, TLC\n2. Run TLC against the spec\n\nThis isn't building anything, and could equally be a shell-script. `make` provides the UI for describing dependencies between actions, and we need a copy of TLC before we can run TLC against the spec. That's all this achieves."
                }
            ],
